{title: O That Will Be Glory}
{artist: Charles Gabriel}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 96}

Verse 1
When [Bb]all my labors and trials are o'er, and [Eb]I am safe on that [Bb]beautiful shore,
just to be near the dear Lord I adore will [C]through the ages be [F]glory for me.

Chorus
O [Bb]that will be [F]glory for [Bb]me, [Eb]glory for [Bb]me, [F]glory for [Bb]me:
when by his grace I shall [Eb]look on his [Bb]face, that will be [F]glory, be [Bb]glory for me.
